persist-thread-settings-without-runtime

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: persist-thread-settings-without-runtime

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Persist unloaded thread model, reasoning effort and cwd without starting a conversation runtime.

Requires: none

Provides: The existing thread/settings/update API checkpoints these sparse edits through native configuration, managed settings constraints, writer ownership and rollout persistence, acknowledges unchanged edits, and leaves the thread unloaded.

Boundary: Loaded requests retain native live settings behavior; all other setting fields retain their loaded-thread requirement. Actual resume, Guardian execution, archive, naming and user configuration remain with their existing owners.

Verification: App-server unloaded_settings_persist_without_starting_a_session legacy and paginated cases verify durable restart and repeated edits, unchanged rollout prefix, no additional session files or loaded runtimes, and unchanged approval policy and reviewer on actual resume; native live-settings and resume configuration tests cover retained paths.


